From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] linux 7.2: set dev_addr through eth_hw_addr_set

Kernel 5.17 made dev_addr const and tracks a shadow copy that drivers
must update through eth_hw_addr_set(). Direct writes trigger the
"Incorrect netdev->dev_addr" warning when wpa_supplicant changes the
MAC address.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/os_dep/linux/os_intfs.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/os_intfs.c
@@ -1776,7 +1776,11 @@
 	}
 
 	_rtw_memcpy(adapter_mac_addr(padapter), sa->sa_data, ETH_ALEN); /* set mac addr to adapter */
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(5, 17, 0))
+	eth_hw_addr_set(pnetdev, sa->sa_data); /* keep dev_addr shadow in sync */
+#else
 	_rtw_memcpy(pnetdev->dev_addr, sa->sa_data, ETH_ALEN); /* set mac addr to net_device */
+#endif
 
 	rtw_hal_set_hw_macaddr(padapter, sa->sa_data);
 
